# Wave W17-M (Route 105): tomb rock — a drowned colonnade standing in the lane’s water: broken column drums with their joint lines drawn round them, stone greys dark at the waterline, a little weed on the capitals, foam collar at the base, the sea baked in around it (design: the Sea Tomb’s drowned colonnade stands mid-lane). Route 105’s own rock — columns, not crags: split from Route 106’s dark crag at a glance.
